.cursor

# Agent-host scratch: autogenerated per-operator config (e.g. Codex cloud
# environment definitions). Not a repository contract — the authoritative Go
# toolchain floor is the `go` directive in go.mod, enforced by toolchain_test.go.
.codex/

# OS cruft — ignored globally on this machine already, but the repo's own
# .gitignore must not depend on a contributor's global gitignore config.
.DS_Store

# Local review-run output. Files already tracked under docs/reviews remain tracked;
# this only hides newly generated review artifacts.
docs/reviews

# Root build binary only — anchored so new files under cmd/newf/ stay visible to git status.
/newf

# Conventional local output dir for `go build -o bin/`. Ignored for the same reason
# as /newf, and because a binary built on one runner's GOARCH is useless on another.
/bin/

# Repo-local tool and Tectonic caches populated by `make paper`.
.cache/

# Local research substrate (default CLI state per README).
.newf/

# Experiment DB snapshots: the durable record is the sha256 committed in records/runtime.json;
# the file itself is retained locally per the pilot RUNBOOK retention rule.
corpus/experiments/*/records/*.db

# Python bytecode from the corpus authoring-package validators. The validators
# themselves are tracked; their compiled caches are per-interpreter and must not
# enter the manifest hash set.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
